Tidy← {
⍝H Tidy (fn)  
⍝H ∘  Aligns comments nicely in dfn or tradfn source (and code generally),
⍝H    distinguishing between left-hand side (LHS) and right-hand side (RHS) 
⍝H    comments, with the latter aligned tidily. LHS comments by default are
⍝H    those placed before column 40 (See min).
⍝H ∘  Unlike other similar software, it can locate the RHS comments in any 
⍝H    desired column and by default calculates a "best" position, handling 
⍝H    cases where a few code lines are longer than most others. 
⍝H ∘  Handles arbitrary char. vectors of vectors and files, as well as in-workspace 
⍝H    fns and ops.
⍝H ∘  To format code itself, it has two options (neither by default):
⍝H    - refmt: uses dfns ¨refmt¨ (which it copies in), or
⍝H    - pms: uses an internal fn ¨pms¨ which exdents guards and comments in two styles,
⍝H      either a narrower style with minimal spaces per tab or a wide style.
⍝H ----------------------
⍝H {res}← [opts] ∇ [source | sourceFi 1]                 
⍝H   source: [sourceDoc≡2 | sourceFnOp≡1 | sourceFi≡1]
⍝H   [sourceFi 1]: Equivalent to: (fi: 1) ∇ sourceFi 
⍝H   opts:
⍝H      col: 'best'    What column should RHS comments preferably be placed in?
⍝H                     ∘ 'best': Place RHS comments at 90th pctile of line lengths.
⍝H                     ∘  dd:   Place at absolute column dd, dd a non-negative number.
⍝H                     ∘  '-nn' '+nn' '×n.nn': Place relative to longest line.
⍝H                     Col numbers will be rounded. Interacts with other options.
⍝H      min: 40        Comments starting at column < min are treated as LHS 
⍝H           dd>0      and never moved. Those at min or greater are RHS comments.
⍝H                     Using (min:40) will treat all comments as RHS comments
⍝H                     except those matching pattern '⍝[^\s]'.
⍝H      fi: 0* |1      If 1, a depth 1/0 right arg (⍵) refers to a file, not a fn or op.
⍝H      updt: 0        If 1, updates the file, fn, or op IN PLACE as side effect.
⍝H            bool     The update will always be returned as a char vec of vectors.
⍝H      double: 1      If 1, we support "double" comments on a single line.
⍝H      inc: 5         If a comment can't fit where desired, place <inc> chars to right, etc.
⍝H      pctile: 95     When (col: 'best'), place just after 95th pctile of line lengths,
⍝H                     i.e. only 1 in 20 code lines will extend beyond start of RHS comments.
⍝H      compact: 50    If (col: 'best') and a object fits in a width of 50 chars, place 
⍝H               >0    RHS comments to the right of all lines, ignoring pctile. (Prettier).
⍝H                     With (col: 'best' ⋄ min: 0), a large value for compact will force
⍝H                     ALL comments to the right (see (min: 0) above).
⍝H      marg: 3 5      What margin (spaces) must there be between code and comments?
⍝H                     [0] For non-compact objects; [1] for compact objs.
⍝H                     Specifying a single number will address BOTH cases.
⍝H      refmt: 0       If >0, calls refmt from the dfns library to format
⍝H            ≥0      the code ONLY; comments are handled by Tidy proper.
⍝H                     To match the dfns refmt, specify:
⍝H                        refmt: 4 
⍝H                     The value is passed to refmt as its first option, 
⍝H                     its tab setting (see dfns notes.refmt).
⍝H      pms: 0         If 0, does nothing. If 1 or 2, calls PmsFmtC with 
⍝H           0|1|2     that value, which formats code just as PMS wants it. 
⍝H                     Pms format exdents comments and guards (to make them easier
⍝H                     to see in a dfn, among other things). 
⍝H                     It has a narrow indent mode (1) and a wide indent mode (2).
⍝H   res: returns the modified source document as a shy char vector of vectors. 
⍝H        See (updt: 1) for side effect.
⍝⍝ For the rest of this HELP info, see bottom of this function or do Tidy⍨'help' 
   DEBUG← 1                                  
  11 22 911/⍨ ~DEBUG::     ⎕SIGNAL⊂⎕DMX.('EN'EN ⋄ 'Message'Message)
⍝  Initialise
   ⎕IO ⎕ML← 0 1
   ⍺← ()
  'help'≡ ⎕C⍺:     ⎕ED 'h'⊣ h← '^\s*⍝H\s?(.*)' ⎕S ' \1'⊢ ⎕NR ⊃⎕XSI 
⍝-------------------------------⍝
⍝  Phase I - Potential Retabsion ⍝
⍝-------------------------------⍝   
⍝  Default Options (Merged with User Options below) 
   o← (                                          
     col:     'best' ⋄ min:     40  ⋄ fi:       0 ⋄ updt: 0   ⋄ double:    1  
     inc:     5      ⋄ pctile:  95  ⋄ compact: 50 ⋄ marg: 3 5 ⋄ refmt:     0  
     pms:     0 
   ) 
⍝  Phase I Errors
   optÊ←   ⊂( 'EN'  11 ⋄ 'Message' 'Unknown option(s)' )
   fnOpÊ←  ⊂( 'EN'  11 ⋄ 'Message' 'Unknown function or operator' )
   fixÊ←   ⊂( 'EN'  11 ⋄ 'Message' 'Can''t fix object' )     
⍝  Phase I Fns  
   ∆Tidy← ∇                                          ⍝ This function ("me")
   FOF← {                                            ⍝ FOF: in-ws Fn/Op or File?
      o.fi ∨← 1≡ ⊃⌽⍵                                 ⍝ Alt way to set o.fi via ⍵
      fi← ⊃⊆,⍵ 
     o.fi:     _← GetFi fi ⋄ 1:     _← GetFnOp fi   
   }
   GetFi← {                                          ⍝ File with code of any type
      ll← o ∆Tidy ⊃⎕NGET ⍵ 1                         ⍝ Get file lines & then tidy
      _← ll⊂⍛⎕NPUT⍣o.updt⊢ ⍵ 1                       ⍝ Update the file. (if o.updt=1) 
     1:     _← ll                                    ⍝ Return shyly.
   }
   GetFnOp← {                                        ⍝ In-ws fn or op
     ~⍵ ⎕NC⍛∊ 3 4:  ⎕SIGNAL fnOpÊ
      ll← o ∆Tidy 62 ⎕ATX ⍵                          ⍝ Get fn/op lines & then tidy. 
     ~o.updt:     _← ll                              ⍝ No update here. Return the lines.
     0≠ ⊃0⍴⎕FX ll:     _← ll                         ⍝ Update the fn/op. Return the lines..
      ⎕SIGNAL fixÊ 
   }
⍝  Phase I Executive 
  ×≢⊃~/(⍺ o).⎕NL ¯2: ⎕SIGNAL optÊ                    ⍝ Validate user-specified options 
   _← o ⎕NS ⍺                                        ⍝ Now merge user options ⍺ into o.
   linesIn← ↓⍣(⊃2=⍴⍴⍵)⊢ ⍵
⍝  If ⍵ is a fn, op, or file name, recurse back to Tidy via FOF.
  (2> ≡linesIn)∨ 0≠ 80| ⎕DR⊃⌽⍵:  FOF linesIn      
⍝--------------------------⍝
⍝  Phase II - No Recursion  ⍝      
⍝--------------------------⍝   
⍝  Phase II Constants
⍝  Error Msgs         
   colÊ←   ⊂( 'EN'  11 ⋄ 'Message' 'Invalid column value' )
   logicÊ← ⊂( 'EN' 911 ⋄ 'Message' 'Logic error (Tidy)' )   
⍝  Phase II Functions  
⍝  RefmtC: 
⍝  Conditionally call dfns ¨refmt¨ to reformat code,
⍝  without impacting comments (handled here by Tidy itself).
⍝  Only useful for dfns, not tradfns or namespaces.
⍝  This "hides" comments so that Tidy handles ALL comments.
⍝  Self-contained...
   RefmtC← { 
      ⍺← 0 ⋄ refmtOpts← ⍺ 
     0= refmtOpts:  ⍵                                ⍝ Nop if 0= refmtOpts (default).                                    
      refmt← ⊢  ⋄  _← 'refmt' ⎕CY 'dfns'             ⍝ Localise refmt from dfns ws.
      qL qR← '''[^'']*''' '&'                        ⍝ Skip quotes
      H← qL '\h*⍝.*' ⎕R qR '\x{00}⍝&'                ⍝ "Hide" comments/leading spaces behind NUL
      UnH← qL '\x{00}\h*⍝(.*)$' ⎕R qR '\1'           ⍝ "Unhide" comments            
      UnH refmtOpts refmt H  ⍵                       ⍝ Unhide after refmt after hide cm/sp
   }
⍝  PmsFmtC: 
⍝  Conditionally provides special PMS-specific formatting (if ⍺=1).
⍝  Self-contained.     
   PmsFmtC← ().{ ⍝⍝ (Note: In its own namespace to hide local names).
      ⎕IO ⎕ML← 0 1
      ⍺← 0 ⋄ wid min← ⍺, 0 40↑⍨ 0⌊2-⍨≢⍺              ⍝ ⍺ is set to o.(pms min)                          
     0=wid:     ⍵    
   ⍝  Updt line padding for this line and...
      TOKNONE←  0                                    ⍝  ... Skip only if last updt already rec'd.  
      TOKLAST←  1                                    ⍝  ... Mark this as last updt for this line.
      TOKFORCE← 2                                    ⍝  ... Updt this line anyway...  
   ⍝  Tab position for different match types (in two variants-- choose one below)
      nms mulNarrow mulWide← ↓⍉↑(                    ⍝ How much to in/exdent constructs..
         'group'      3   6                          ⍝ (indent) inside a {([])} group    
         'guard'     ¯1  ¯3                          ⍝ (exdent) group with guard 
         'cmLine'    ¯3  ¯3                          ⍝ (exdent) LHS comments  
         'tradFn'     3   3                          ⍝ (indent) trad functions
         'ctrlIf'     3   3                          ⍝ (indent) :IF, :WHILE, :SELECT 
         'ctrlElse'  ¯3  ¯3                          ⍝ (exdent) elseif, else
         'ctrlCase'  ¯2  ¯2                          ⍝ (exdent) Case stmts 
      )
      _← ⎕VSET (↑nms) (⍳≢nms)                        ⍝ Load in local names (indices)
   ⍝  indices of parms in ¨tab¨ that are reset after each line.
      resetL← guard cmLine ctrlElse ctrlCase 
   ⍝  "standard" multiplier is mulNarrow (above)
      mulV← mulNarrow mulWide⊃⍨ 2=wid                ⍝ # of spaces for each type of tab (group, guard, etc.)    
      tabV← 0⍨¨ mulV                                 ⍝ count of each type of tab            
   ⍝  Generate key patterns and their names (pattern #s)  
      cmLftP←     '^(?:\h{0,', m2, '}⍝|\h*⍝⍝).*'⊣ m2← ⍕0⌈ min- 2 
      cmSectBP← '(?i)^\h*⍝\h*:Section.*$'            ⍝ Section embedded in comments...
   ⍝  Must match: 
   ⍝    Namespace | Section | If | Repeat | For | Select | While | Trap With | Hold 
      ctrlIfP← ':\w+'                                ⍝ Follows ALL other ctrl patterns
      ctrlElseP← '(?i):(?|Else|And|Or)\w*' 
      ctrlCaseP← '(?i):Case\w*'
      ctrlEndP← '(?i):(?:End\w*|Until)'
      cmSectEP← '(?i)^\h*⍝\h*:End\w*.*$' 
      pats pNames← ↓⍉↑(            
      ⍝  Ordered patterns. Some like ctrlIfP matches anything not in prior ctrl Pats
      ⍝  Pattern              PatName      ⋄  ⍝ Pattern         PatName    
         '^'                  'newline'    ⋄  '^\h*∇\h*(⍝.*)?$' 'tradE'    
      ⍝  tradB will be treated as ∇ function, if inside a dfn.
         '^\h*∇(?!∇)'         'tradB'      ⋄  cmSectBP          'cmSectB'   
         cmSectEP             'cmSectE'    ⋄  cmLftP            'cmLft'         
         '\h?⋄\h?'            'dmnd'       ⋄  '^\h+'            'spLft'     
         ctrlEndP             'ctrlEnd'    ⋄  ctrlElseP         'ctrlElse'     
         ctrlCaseP            'ctrlCase'   ⋄  ctrlIfP           'ctrlB'    
         '''[^'']*'''         'qt'         ⋄  '[[{(]+'          'grpB'  
         '[]})]+'             'grpE'       ⋄  '::?\h?'          'guard'    
         '⍝.*'                'cm'         ⋄  '←(?!\h)'         'assign'   
      )
   ⍝  pat: Pattern "names" refer to their pattern numbers. 
   ⍝      I.e. pat.newLine← 0  ⋄  pat.assign← ¯1+≢pats 
      pat← ().⎕VSET (↑pNames) (⍳≢pats) 
      ⍝ :Section Support Functions  
         DLB← ##.DLB 
         TradB←  { inDfn← ⍵
           inDfn: ⍺  
            ⍺ ⊣ tabV[tradFn]+← 1 ⊣ Tok TOKLAST 
         }   
         TradE← { inDfn← ⍵  
           inDfn: ⍺ 
            ⍺ ⊣ Tok TOKLAST ⊣ tabV[tradFn]-←  1  
         }
         Guard← { f0 skip← ⍺ ⍵                                      
            f0,← ''↑⍨' '≠⊃⌽f0                        ⍝ Ensure at least one space after guard...
            tabV[guard]⊢← skip=0
           tabV[guard]: f0⊣ Tok TOKFORCE+TOKLAST ⋄ f0 ⍝ Guard inside one-line dfn def is ignored.
         } 
         Newline← {
            tabV[resetL]⊢← updtFlg⊢← grpCt⊢← 0       ⍝ Turned off before each line   
            ⊢ pfxStk,← ⊂⊃⌽CalcTab⍬
         } 
         Tok← { force last← 2 2⊤⍵
           updtFlg∧ ~force: 0                        ⍝ Skip: Line already fully updated.
            (⊃⌽pfxStk)⊢← CalcTab⍬ 
            ⊢ updtFlg∨← last 
         }
         CalcTab← { ∧/ 0= tabV: 0 ⋄ 0⌈ +/tabV × mulV }
         Debug← {
           ~⍺: ⍬
            ⎕← 'Blk: "','"',⍨⍵.Block 
            ⎕← ∊(
               10↑ ⍵.PatternNum⊃pNames ⋄  33↑'"', '" ',⍨ {30>≢⍵: ⍵ 
               '...',⍨27↑⍵} ⍵.Match    ⋄  12∘↑¨ (b/nms),¨ ':',¨ ⍕¨(b← 1= tabV)/ tabV 
               'grpCt:', ⍕grpCt 
            )
            ⍬
         }
      ⍝ :EndSection Support Functions 
   ⍝  Main Routine
      updtFlg← 0                                     ⍝ Has the pfxStk already been updated for this line?
      grpCt← 0                                       ⍝ The # of grouping elements {([])} seen on THIS line
      pfxStk← ⍬                                      ⍝ Our main result-- how many blanks to prefix to each line 
      
      Scan← pats ⎕R {
         Case← ⍵.PatternNum∘∊
         f0← ⍵.Match
         _← 0 Debug ⍵ 
         
        Case pat.newline:   ''      ⊣ Newline ⍬ 
        Case pat.cmLft:     DLB f0  ⊣ Tok TOKNONE ⊣ tabV[cmLine]⊢← 1   
        Case pat.spLft:     ''      ⊣ Tok TOKNONE   
         
        Case pat.(qt cm):   f0
        Case pat.assign:    f0,' ' 
        Case pat.dmnd:      p, f0, q ⊣ (p q)← ' '↑⍨¨' '≠ (⊃f0) (⊃⌽f0) 
         
        Case pat.grpB:      f0 ⊣ tabV[group]+← grpCt+← ≢f0⊣ Tok TOKLAST
        Case pat.grpE:      f0 ⊣ Tok TOKNONE ⊣ tabV[group]-← grpCt-← ≢f0 
        Case pat.guard:     f0 Guard grpCt  
         
        Case pat.tradB:     f0 DLB⍛TradB tabV[group]>0  
        Case pat.tradE:     f0 DLB⍛TradE tabV[group]>0 
         
        Case pat.ctrlB:     f0      ⊣ tabV[ctrlIf]+← 1 ⊣ Tok TOKLAST
        Case pat.cmSectB:   DLB f0  ⊣ tabV[ctrlIf]+← 1 ⊣ Tok TOKLAST  
         
        Case pat.ctrlElse:  f0      ⊣ Tok TOKLAST ⊣ tabV[ctrlElse]⊢←  1     
        Case pat.ctrlCase:  f0      ⊣ Tok TOKLAST ⊣ tabV[ctrlCase]⊢←  1
        Case pat.ctrlEnd:   f0      ⊣ Tok TOKLAST ⊣ tabV[ctrlIf]-←  1  
        Case pat.cmSectE:   DLB f0  ⊣ Tok TOKLAST ⊣ tabV[ctrlIf]-←  1  
         
         'Logic Error (PmsFmtC)' ⎕SIGNAL 911
      }  
      (pfxStk⍴¨' '),¨ Scan ⍵  
   }
   
   AL← {                                             ⍝ AL: Align line
      ∆ p← ⍺ ⍵                                       ⍝ ∆: Pad by at least ∆ spaces. 
     p≤o.col:     ''⍴⍨ ∆⌈ ¯1+ o.col- p        
      ''⍴⍨ ∆⌈ ¯1+ o.inc| p- o.col       
   }
   AC← { ⍺← ⊢ ⋄ o.min⌈ ⌊0.5+ ⍺ AC_main ⍵ }           ⍝ AC: Generate Absolute col  
   ⍝ :Section AC Main Routine
      AC_main← {                                     ⍝ AC Main Routine
        0=⊃0⍴⍺: ⍺                                    ⍝ Fast-- col is a number 
         LL← {                                       ⍝ LL: adjusted line length for RHS comments
            P← {                                     ⍝ Pctile (rounded)
               i← 100÷⍨p×¯1+≢⍵ 
               R 0.5× ⍵[⌊i]+ ⍵[⌈i] 
            }
            R← ⌊0.5∘+                                ⍝ Round                       
            S← ⊂∘⍋⍛⌷                                 ⍝ Sort 
            ⍺← 100                                   ⍝ ⍺/p: What %age of ll. 
            pic← 0                                   ⍝ pic: include comments in pctile calc
            p isB← ⍺ ⍺⍺                              ⍝ p: position, isB: 'best' option 
            trimI trimO← ↓⍉↑1 pic 1 1/(       
               '''[^'']*''' '&'
               ('\s{0,', m2,'}⍝.*$') '&'⊣ m2← ⍕0⌈ o.min- 2   ⍝ pic=1: include comments in pctile calc
               '\s*⍝.*$'    ''
               '\s*$'       ''
            )                      
            max← ⌈/ll← ≢¨trimI ⎕R trimO⊢ ⍵           ⍝ trimmed line lengths 
           ~isB:    max                              ⍝ Abs. position needed. Else isBest ↓↓↓
            isC← max≤ o.compact                      ⍝ Is the object compact?
            marg← isC⊃ 2⍴o.marg 
           isC:     marg+ max                        ⍝ Obj is compact, "best" is on the right.
           p≥ 100:  marg+ R 0.01× p× max             ⍝ % (not %ile) if above 100% 
            marg+ P S ll                             ⍝ Actual interpolated percentile + margin
         } 
         V←  ⊃∘⌽∘⎕VFI                                ⍝ Value
      ⍝  "Best" line length is  o.pctile-th %ile of input line lengths.
         f← ⊃⍺                                       ⍝ Selector is first char...
      ⍝  col set to "best" line length plus margin.
        f∊ 'bB':    o.pctile (1 LL) ⍵                ⍝ "best" must be at least o.min.
        f∊ '+-×':    ((0 LL) ⍵) (⍎f) V 1↓⍺           ⍝ col is relative to exact max line length.
        0∊⊃⎕VFI ⍺:  ⎕SIGNAL colÊ
         V ⍺                                         ⍝ Absolute positioning
      }
   ⍝ :EndSection AC Main Routine
   
   TB← { +/∧\' '= ⌽⍵ }                               ⍝ TB: Trailing blanks
   LB← { +/∧\' '=  ⍵ }                               ⍝ LB: Leading blanks 
   DLB← { ⍵↓⍨ +/∧\' '=  ⍵ }
   RF← {                                             ⍝ RF: Regex Field value
      ⍺.Lengths[⍵]↑ ⍺.Offsets[⍵]↓ ⍺.Block 
   } 
⍝  Helper Functions for fn FmtComments             
   CmProc← { m← ⍵    
      nsp← LB m                                      ⍝ cmI:  Std comments 
     o.min> cur+ nsp:  m                             ⍝ LHS cm: return as is
      (1 AL cur), nsp↓ m                             ⍝ RHS cm: align and pad
   }
   Cm2Proc← { ns← ⍵                                  ⍝ "Double" comments (see doc)
      cm1 cm2← ns RF¨ 1 2                            ⍝ ... Get LHS and RHS comments
      cm1↓⍨← -TB cm1                                 ⍝ ... Remove trail. blanks from LHS...
      padL← 5 AL cur+ ≢cm1                           ⍝ ... Align "2nd" comment on RHS
      cm1, padL, cm2                                 ⍝ ... and pad 
   }
⍝-----------------------------⍝
⍝  Main Executive (Phase IIa)  ⍝
⍝-----------------------------⍝ 
⍝  Executive - Variable/Constant Declarations  
   cur← 0                                            ⍝ cur: Our cur pos'n on this line.                                 
   o.col← o.col AC ⍵                                 ⍝ Calculate the absolute col pos'n.
   nlI cdI lcI cm2I cmI spI← ⍳≢pats← (               ⍝ Our patterns...
      '^'                                            ⍝ nlI:  start    (of line)
      '''[^'']*''|[^⍝''\s]+'                         ⍝ cdI:  code     (fragments)
      '\s*⍝\S.*$'                                    ⍝ lcI:  literal comment (don't format)
      o.double⊃ (                                    ⍝ cm2I: double comments
         '(*F)'                                      ⍝ Ignore dbl comments                                      
         '(\s*⍝.+?\s{5,})((?<!⍝)⍝(?!\S).*)$'         ⍝    ← active pattern. ≥5 spaces between   
      )      
      '\s*⍝.*$'                                      ⍝ cmI:  comment  (w/ preceding spaces)
      '\s+(?!⍝)'                                     ⍝ spI:  spaces (not before comments)
   )
⍝  Executive - Pattern Matching Scan 
   FmtComments← pats ⎕R {  
      m← ⍵.Match 
      Case← ⍵.PatternNum∘=
     Case nlI:      m ⊣ cur⊢← 0                      ⍝ Start of new line
     Case cdI:      m ⊣ cur+← ≢m                     ⍝ Code found
     Case lcI:      m ⊣ cur+← ≢m                     ⍝ literal comment '⍝⍝'
     Case spI:      m ⊣ cur+← ≢m                     ⍝ Spaces (not foll by comment)
     Case cm2I:     Cm2Proc ⍵                        ⍝ Double comment. ⍵=this ns 
     Case cmI:      CmProc m                         ⍝ Simple comment. ⍵=current match
      ⎕SIGNAL logicÊ                                 ⍝  →→  Error!
   } 
   ↑⍣(⊃2=⍴⍴⍵)⊢ FmtComments o.(pms min)∘PmsFmtC o.refmt∘RefmtC linesIn  
   
⍝   Rest of "help" information
⍝H ---------------------------------
⍝H Other features:
⍝H ¯¯¯¯¯ ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯
⍝H ∘ Allows "double" comments, i.e. those with both a LHS comment
⍝H   (starting with ⍝) and a RHS comment (a second ⍝). (See double: 1)
⍝H ∘ Can place comments in the "best" position, where some code lines
⍝H   are far longer than the average. (See col: 'best')
⍝H ∘ LHS comments are never moved.
⍝H ∘ RHS comments that start with ⍝⍝ or ⍝X, where X is any non-space, are never moved,
⍝H   even within "double" comments.
⍝H ∘ If the longest lines are shorter than ¨compact¨ number of bytes,
⍝H   (compact: 50) by default, the "best" position will be just to the 
⍝H   right of ALL lines, as for ¨refmt¨ in the dfns library.   
⍝H   (See compact and marg options).
⍝H ---------------------------------
⍝H Documentation: 
⍝H ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯
⍝H   To see this information, call: Tidy⍨'help'  
⍝H
}
